			<td align="center">
				<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="5" align="center">
				<b>The Media's Silence of the Lambs over the Palestinian Non-violent movement</b></font>
			</td>
		</tr><tr><td><hr height="1"></td></tr>
		<tr>
            <td height="304"> 
              <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">We have all 
			  read them: editorials and columns bemoaning a lack among Palestinians
			  of a non-violent reistence, calls from experts and talking heads on 
			  Palestinians to find another way to resist beside the militant one, 
			  accusations from all corners that the Palestinians lack a real
			  strategy, etc. etc.  
			  </font></p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">Anyone who is in any way seriously familiar with the Palestinian
			  struggle knows full well that a long tradition of non-violent 
			  resistance does exist, and more importantly, that a momentum
			  of non-violence has been steadily building since the start
			  of the second intifada.  And yet, the media has hardly talked
			  about it, the so-called gurus have rarely if ever focused their
			  spotlight on it, instead, what we have had is a complicit silence --
			  a SILENCE OF THE LAMBS -- on the non-violent movement.  No one talks
			  about it, preferring instead to do the usual safe thing: the same 
			  bemoaning, the same wringing of the hands, the same blaming
			  of the victims, as if there were no alternative.
			  </font></p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">Please impress upon the media the need to highlight the growing
			  non-violent movement.  The article below is a piece by Prof. Edward
			  Said that talks about this emerging new force -- a force that Ariel
			  Sharon and his deadly weaponry can do NOTHING against.  As Prof Said
			  says, Mustafa Barghouti is probably much more terrifying to Ariel
			  Sharon than any suicide bomber.
			  </font></p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">Please help us pass the word around.  Pick the paper of your choice 
			  below, fill your personal information, add your comments, and then click send. 
              </font></p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">Palestine 
                Media Watch - <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/index.html" class="dead" aria-disabled="true">http://www.pmwatch.org</a></font></font></p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">
